[h1]Phobos Agriculture[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.20.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - development candidate

A hot meal is a useful thing to come home to. Grow potatoes and lettuce aboard with Verdemorrow Agronomics equipment, cook potato portions in the galley, and keep the water and nutrients going between stations.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Phobos' Verdemorrow Firstlight-4 Cultivation Rack[/b] (4 x 4): grows potatoes, food lettuce or a separate lettuce seed crop. The four trays show the crop growing and share one crop cycle.
[*][b]Phobos' Verdemorrow Hearth-2 Galley Cooker[/b] (2 x 2): cooks one 0.4 kg potato portion per Start.
[*]Start with manual water and nutrient charges. Add a Groundwork W2 Water Supply Unit and irrigation pipes for up to eight racks, then an optional R3, R4 or R5 water reservoir (120, 235 or 400 kg) within one tile of the W2.
[*]The Groundwork B2 Workup Bench recovers nutrients from recorded crop residue; add makeup salts and use the mixture in the W2.
[*]Crew orders can plant, haul supplies, harvest and cook. An optional quiet alert tells you when a meal or crop is ready.
[*]Buy agricultural water and 500 g nutrient charges through the station Bulk supplies view. Review each quote before buying.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[list]
[*]Buy equipment, seed potatoes, lettuce seeds and nutrients at supply kiosks, the fixer or suitable general traders; used, refurbished and broken machines turn up too. Or build the rack and cooker at an installed Bar or Dining Table with a screwdriver and soldering tools. Some supplies appear in newly generated fridges and crates.
[*]Install the rack and cooker on cabin floor and connect power. Keep the room at 18 to 26 C and 70 to 110 kPa, with some CO2 in the air.
[*]Right-click the rack, put a seed potato or seed packet, an irrigation charge and nutrients in its Inventory, load them, then choose Plant. Harvest when the panel says the crop is ready.
[*]In the F3 console, phobosagriculture list shows your equipment.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.44.0 or newer.
[*]BepInEx 5 through EddieSM / EsMM27's [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3741030124]BepInEx Mod Loader[/url], including its one-time setup.
[*]Optional: Phobos Shipbreaker for C1 console control and T2 thaw water into an R3; Valtora's Ship's Water 0.16.1 as a water supply. Manual supplies always remain available.
[/list]

[h2]Installing from the Workshop[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to the BepInEx Mod Loader and follow its setup instructions.
[*]Subscribe to Phobos Agriculture and the Phobos items listed under Required items.
[*]Start Ostranauts once so the loader copies the plugins, then restart it once so they load. Do the same after each update.
[*]Check that the mods are enabled in the MODS screen.
[*]Used the repository's local installer before? Remove those local copies first so only one copy loads. See the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/installing-mods.md]installation guide[/url].
[/list]

[h2]Saves and limits[/h2]
Ordinary saves are supported. Keep required mods installed while a save uses their content. Updating does not refill existing shops or old loot containers. After a reload, resume cultivation or cooking and water receiving separately.
Supplies, output space, cabin conditions and power matter. Food lettuce gives no seeds. Treated drainage is never drinking water, and Recycler wet rejects have no fertilizer recipe. Growth times, yields and simplified chemistry are gameplay choices, not NASA or ESA results. Automated checks pass; in-game evaluation of the complete loop is ongoing.

[h2]Credits and sources[/h2]
Created by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko). Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games, Kitfox Games or the research institutions cited below. Research informs design; compact equipment, yields and operating limits remain gameplay choices.
NASA plant work and ESA's MELiSSA programme inform the crop and recovery research. [url=https://extension.okstate.edu/fact-sheets/hydroponics]Bruce Dunn, Oklahoma State University[/url] informs hydroponics; [url=https://technology.nasa.gov/patent/ksc-tops-73]NASA porous-tube research[/url] informs root-water delivery; [url=https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19930008922]Jay Garland of Bionetics, NASA TM-107557[/url] informs nutrient recovery. The research guide separates findings from our simplified recipes.
Optional integrations remain their authors' work: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3757331189]Valtora's Ship's Water[/url], [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3789049955]LOGUSS's Common Sense modules[/url] and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3788237703]jossla's Study at Terminals[/url]. Linking does not imply endorsement.
Original artwork uses AI-assisted production; provenance and licensing are recorded separately.

